<title>CHINA: China's Xinhua Insurance '96 premium over 260 mln.</title>
<headline>China's Xinhua Insurance '96 premium over 260 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Xinhua Life Insurance Co Ltd reported income from life insurance premiums of more than 260 million yuan ($31.33 million) in 1996, the Financial News said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Xinhua Life Insurance Co was founded in Beijing on August 20 1996. Its registered capital was 500 million yuan, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The company would apply in the second half of the year to the People's Bank of China, the central bank, to open new branches outside Beijing, it quoted company officials as saying.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>--Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
